# Label templates are byte-exact by definition. They carry CRLF line endings
# because that is what a Zebra printer is given, and the proxy seeds them into
# config/labels/ and checks them against a known checksum. Letting git rewrite
# the line endings on checkout would change those bytes on Windows and break
# both the checksum and, potentially, the print.
*.zpl -text
*.prn -text
